        "Content": "Special Features – 30 Father Murphy Square\r\n•\tSuperbly presented and extensively upgraded two-storey home in turn-key condition – ready for immediate occupation \r\n•\tBright and welcoming entrance hallway with modern flooring \r\n•\tComfortable front living room with feature solid-fuel stove \r\n•\tBeautifully upgraded kitchen/dining room with contemporary shaker-style fitted kitchen with integrated appliances \r\n•\tLarge rooflight providing excellent natural light to the kitchen \r\n•\tGround-floor fully tiled bathroom with bath and overhead shower \r\n•\tTwo well-proportioned bedrooms \r\n•\tPrincipal bedroom benefits from a modern en-suite \r\n•\tAdditional first-floor room currently arranged as a home office \r\n•\tPrivate cobblelock driveway providing off-street parking \r\n•\tAttractive, well-maintained front façade with mature hedging \r\n•\tSuperb rear patio and outdoor entertaining area, Low-maintenance rear garden with artificial lawn and paved areas, \r\n        Excellent space for outdoor dining, BBQs and seating \r\n•\tDetached outbuilding/workshop, offering valuable storage and versatility \r\n•\tSecure and private rear boundaries \r\n•\tSeparate utility room with laundry facilities and direct garden access \r\n•\tProperty has benefited from significant investment and thoughtful upgrading \r\n•\tAn ideal walk-in home suitable for owner-occupiers or investment purchasers \r\n\r\n30 Father Murphy Square is a superbly presented and extensively upgraded two-storey home, offering a stylish, contemporary interior, excellent outdoor space and a highly practical layout. The quality of the finish throughout is immediately apparent, making this a genuine walk-in opportunity where much of the hard work has already been completed.\r\nExternally, the property presents particularly well. A cobblelock driveway to the front provides valuable private off-street parking. The clean rendered façade, contrasting window surrounds and smart entrance give No. 30 an attractive and well-maintained appearance.\r\nStepping inside, the entrance hallway immediately sets the tone for the rest of the house. Warm timber-effect flooring, contemporary décor and a carpeted staircase create a welcoming first impression, with the accommodation flowing naturally from here.\r\nThe living room is positioned to the front of the house and is a comfortable, well-proportioned reception space. A large front window provides excellent natural light, while the feature fireplace with solid-fuel stove creates an attractive focal point and adds greatly to the cosy feel of the room. Recessed lighting, display shelving and modern flooring complete this inviting space.\r\nTo the rear lies one of the real highlights of the property – the beautifully upgraded kitchen and dining room. This is a bright and exceptionally well-finished space, fitted with an extensive range of contemporary shaker-style units in a rich green finish, complemented by light worktops and integrated appliances. A large rooflight floods the kitchen with natural light, while the generous proportions comfortably accommodate a substantial dining table, creating an excellent everyday family and entertaining space.\r\nOff the kitchen is a separate utility room, a hugely practical addition to any home. It provides dedicated laundry facilities and worktop space, while a large rooflight adds further natural light. A door from here gives direct access to the rear garden.\r\nAlso located on the ground floor is a fully tiled bathroom, finished in a contemporary neutral palette and fitted with a bath and overhead electric shower, WC and wash-hand basin.\r\nThe first floor continues the same well-maintained standard. The principal bedroom is a generous double room positioned to the front and benefits from excellent natural light and a modern en-suite. The en-suite itself has been particularly well finished, with contemporary tiling, sanitary ware and modern fittings.\r\nA second comfortable bedroom is located to the rear, while an additional room is presently arranged as a home office. This flexibility is a particularly attractive feature for purchasers working from home and offers scope for alternative use depending on individual requirements. The floor plan indicates approximately 350 sq. ft. of accommodation at first-floor level, with approximately 466 sq. ft. at ground-floor level.\r\nThe outside space at No. 30 is another major selling feature. Immediately to the rear of the house is a superbly finished patio and entertaining area, providing ample room for outdoor dining, seating and barbecuing. The garden has been designed with low maintenance in mind, incorporating artificial lawn areas, paved pathways and secure boundary walls. The result is an extremely usable and private outdoor space requiring minimal upkeep.\r\nBeyond the landscaped garden lies a further substantial concrete yard with a detached outbuilding/workshop measuring 15’9” X 19’5”. This additional space considerably enhances the property's versatility, providing excellent storage and potential for workshop, hobby or other ancillary uses.\r\nFor purchasers seeking a home where modern finishes, practicality and generous outside space come together, No. 30 represents an excellent opportunity and viewing is highly recommended. The supplied virtual tour for the property is available here: 30 Father Murphy Square virtual tour.\r\n\r\n\r\nThese particulars are issued strictly on the understanding that they do not form part of any contract and are provided, without liability, as a general guide only to what is being offered, subject to contract and availability. They are not to be constructed as containing any representation of fact upon which any interested party is entitled to rely. Any intending purchaser or lessee should satisfy themselves by inspection or otherwise as to the accuracy of these particulars. The vendor or lessor do not make, give or imply nor is Fran Grincell Properties or its staff authorized to make, give or imply any representation or warranty whatsoever in respect of this property. No responsibility can be accepted for any expenses incurred by intending purchasers in inspecting properties which have been sold, let or withdrawn. Fran Grincell Properties are advertising this property with the instruction the property certificates and title documents are correct.\r\n*THINKING OF SELLING EMAIL OR CALL FOR SALES ADVICE PACK*"
